    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "389e01d4_f1efdfdd",
        "filename": "vm_payload/include/vm_payload.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T17:18:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, very late comment: we should explain the downsides of enabling tombstones for non-debuggable - there\u0027s a chance the tombstone could leak something sensitive from inside the protected VM, thereby breaching the protection.\n\n(Because really most VMs shouldn\u0027t do this; CompOS does because its secrets are never held anywhere that might be covered and most of what it does can be public.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "e603d6bdd992856867d2e73e79d90476ad1799ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf5f12c5_0084db2f",
        "filename": "vm_payload/include/vm_payload.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T17:01:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we don\u0027t want to give payload an ability to disable the tombstone export, then won\u0027t it make more sense to provide this API on the java layer? I.e. in the VirtualMachineConfig?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "e603d6bdd992856867d2e73e79d90476ad1799ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
